From 44589c285421cbb9f54c8def0ddefa5ce88db329 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work8_fin_tc <adbtrr_work8_fin_tc@local>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 06:15:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] os/kernel/irq: Add ASSERT hitting test case for the irq
 module

g_irq_spin_count[] in os/kernel/irq/irq_spinlock.c counts how deep
spin_lock_irqsave(NULL) is nested on a CPU. spin_unlock_irqrestore()
guards the decrement with DEBUGASSERT(0 < g_irq_spin_count[me]), so an
unbalanced release drives the counter below zero and hits the assertion.

os/kernel/irq/irq_spinlock.c and os/kernel/irq/irq_csection.c hold every
DEBUGASSERT of the module but are only built for CONFIG_SMP. On a single
core build the test case falls back to irq_unexpected_isr(), which takes
the unconditional PANIC() when an unregistered interrupt is dispatched.

 - os/drivers/os_api_test/kernel/test_assert_irq.c : kernel side helper
   reached through the TESTIOC_ASSERT_IRQ ioctl.
 - apps/examples/testcase/le_tc/kernel/tc_assert_irq.c : user side test
   case. A return from the ioctl is reported as a test case failure.

Controlled by CONFIG_TC_KERNEL_ASSERT_IRQ, default n, depends on
CONFIG_DEBUG. It crashes the board by design and must be enabled alone.
